{"path":"algorithm/sample","title":"std::sample","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>sample","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/algorithm/sample","section":"algorithm","kind":"page","summary":"Selects n elements from the sequence [first, last) (without replacement) such that each possible sample has equal probability of appearance, and writes those selected elements into the output iterator out.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/algorithm\">&lt;algorithm&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx17\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> PopulationIt, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> SampleIt, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Distance, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> URBG <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>SampleIterator sample<span class=\"br0\">(</span> PopulationIt first, PopulationIt last,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;SampleIt out, Distance n, URBG<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> g <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx17\">(since C++17)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Selects <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">n</span></code> elements from the sequence <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">first</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">last</span></code><code>)</code></span> (without replacement) such that each possible sample has equal probability of appearance, and writes those selected elements into the output iterator <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">out</span></code>. Random numbers are generated using the random number generator <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">g</span></code>.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">n</span></code> is greater than the number of elements in the sequence, selects all elements in the sequence.\n</p><p>The algorithm is stable (preserves the relative order of the selected elements) only if <code>PopulationIt</code> meets the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/ForwardIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyForwardIterator</em></a>.\n</p><p>If <span class=\"t-rev-inl t-until-cxx20\"><span>the value type of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">first</span></code></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span></span></span><span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx20\"><span><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>first</span></code></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span></span></span> is not <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator#Types_and_writability\">writable</a> to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">out</span></code>, the program is ill-formed.\n</p><p>If any of the following conditions is satisfied, the behavior is undefined:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">out</span></code> is in <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">first</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">last</span></code><code>)</code></span>.\n</li><li> <code>PopulationIt</code> does not meet the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/InputIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyInputIterator</em></a>.\n</li><li> <code>SampleIt</code> does not meet the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/OutputIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyOutputIterator</em></a>.\n</li><li> All following conditions are satisfied:\n</li></ul>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-until-cxx23\"><td>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> <code>PopulationIt</code> does not meet the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/ForwardIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyForwardIterator</em></a>.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx23\">(until C++23)</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-since-cxx23\"><td>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> <code>PopulationIt</code> does not model <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/forward_iterator\"><code>forward_iterator</code></a>.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> <code>SampleIt</code> does not meet the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyRandomAccessIterator</em></a>.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<ul><li> Given the type <code>T</code> as <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_reference\"><span class=\"kw612\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_reference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>URBG<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span>, any of the following conditions is satisfied:\n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> <code>T</code> does not meet the requirements of <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/UniformRandomBitGenerator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">UniformRandomBitGenerator</em></a>.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<table class=\"t-rev-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-rev t-until-cxx20\"><td>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> The return type of <code>T</code> is not convertible to <code>Distance</code>.\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx20\">(until C++20)</span></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> first, last\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pair of iterators forming the range from which to make the sampling (the population)\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> out\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the output iterator where the samples are written\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> n\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> number of samples to make\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> g\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the random number generator used as the source of randomness\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-hitem\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> Type requirements\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par-req\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"> -<div class=\"spacer\"></div><code>Distance</code> must be an integer type.\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Returns a copy of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">out</span></code> after the last sample that was output, that is, end of the sample range.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Linear in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/distance\"><span class=\"kw678\">std::<span class=\"me2\">distance</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>first, last<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Possible_implementation\">Possible implementation</h3>\n<p>See the implementations in <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/blob/14d8a5ae472ca5743016f37da2dd4770d83dea21/libstdc%2B%2B-v3/include/bits/stl_algo.h#L5743-L5869\" data-external=\"1\">libstdc++</a>, <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/f221d905b131158cbe3cbc4320d1ecd1376c3f22/libcxx/include/__algorithm/sample.h\" data-external=\"1\">libc++</a> and <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://github.com/microsoft/STL/blob/472161105d596192194d4715ccad307c6c163b4a/stl/inc/algorithm#L4518-L4600\" data-external=\"1\">MSVC STL</a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This function may implement selection sampling or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/reservoir_sampling\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">reservoir sampling</a>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr></th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr></th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_sample\"><code>__cpp_lib_sample</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/17#cpp_lib_sample_201603L\"><code>201603L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++17)</span></td>\n<td><code>std::sample</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;algorithm&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iterator&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;random&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> in <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"ABCDEFGHIJK\"</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, out<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">sample</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>in.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, in.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/back_inserter\"><span class=\"kw670\">std::<span class=\"me2\">back_inserter</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>out<span class=\"br0\">)</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">4</span>,\n                <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/random/mersenne_twister_engine\"><span class=\"kw1498\">std::<span class=\"me2\">mt19937</span></span></a> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/random/random_device\"><span class=\"kw1495\">std::<span class=\"me2\">random_device</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1774\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Four random letters out of \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> in <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"&nbsp;: \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> out <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Four random letters out of ABCDEFGHIJK: EFGK</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/random_shuffle\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>random_shuffle</span><span>shuffle</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-until-cxx17\">(until C++17)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  randomly re-orders elements in a range <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/sample\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>ranges::sample</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> selects N random elements from a sequence<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(algorithm function object)</span></td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Possible implementation","id":"Possible_implementation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"algorithm","title":"Algorithms library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::sample","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++17. Selects n elements from the sequence [first, last) (without replacement) such that each possible sample has equal…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"first, last, out, n, g"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Returns a copy of out after the last sample that was output, that is, end of the sample range."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Linear in std::distance(first, last)."},{"label":"Possible implementation","note":"See the implementations in libstdc++, libc++ and MSVC STL."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This function may implement selection sampling or reservoir sampling."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"random_shuffle, shuffle","note":"randomly re-orders elements in a range"},{"label":"ranges::sample","note":"selects N random elements from a sequence"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++17","C++20","C++23"],"wordCount":404,"codeBlockCount":2}
